WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.920
Is "Gran Turismo" a green light for other&nbsp;
Playstation game adaptations? Here's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.412
breakdown of the film's high-octane final lap&nbsp;
and what it could mean for a possible franchise.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.760
Before we race to the film's finale, let's recap&nbsp;
the biggest moments leading up to it. After Nissan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:20.340
executive Danny Moore gets approval to create&nbsp;
the competition series "GT Academy" and recruits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.960
bitterly retired racer Jack Salter, he starts&nbsp;
to pick out competitors from across the globe.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.580
British hopeful Jann Mardenborough joins the&nbsp;
competition after earning his spot in a virtual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.720
qualifying race. Although Jann and his fellow&nbsp;
competitors are hopeful that their dreams will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.160
become a reality, Salter gives them a reality&nbsp;
check through some harsh but necessary training.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.020
Despite Salter's tough training methods that push&nbsp;
everyone to their limits, Jann is not only able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.580
to improve his skills but ultimately comes&nbsp;
out victorious by the narrowest of margins.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.517
Before being able to join the ranks&nbsp;
of the world's top racers though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:55.440
Jann must earn his professional license and&nbsp;
contract with Nissan by placing fourth or higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.300
in a qualifying series. Although Jann's first&nbsp;
race doesn't go well, he steadily improves and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.115
is eventually able to place high enough to earn&nbsp;
his license and start his professional career.

00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:09.900
Shortly after signing his contract with Nissan,&nbsp;
Jann enters his first race and even though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.400
things start well, it ends in disaster.&nbsp;
Jann's car unexpectedly flips in the air&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.634
and crashes into a spectator section&nbsp;
-- accidentally killing a spectator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:23.074
This tragedy causes Jann to blame himself for&nbsp;
what happened and give up racing altogether.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.300
Although Salter has his doubts about&nbsp;
Jann and his fellow competitors' ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.320
to actually compete in motorsport, he&nbsp;
slowly starts to see how capable they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.449
are -- especially Jann. By the time&nbsp;
Jann earns his professional license,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.449 --> 00:01:39.868
Salter completely believes in him and&nbsp;
is arguably his biggest supporter.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.361
"I'm not afraid."

00:01:41.361 --> 00:01:42.802
"You should be."

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.440
After Jann's accident though, Salter&nbsp;
is crushed by Jann's decision to quit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:51.180
racing. Salter ultimately decides to reach out&nbsp;
to Jann and take him for a drive back to where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.080
the accident occurred. There, he finally&nbsp;
tells Jann what caused him to stop racing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.837
and it turns out that it's similar&nbsp;
to what Jann is going through.

00:01:57.837 --> 00:02:02.340
Salter was also a part of a tragic accident&nbsp;
at the peak of his career -- which caused a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.540
fatality that he was never able to shake.&nbsp;
Like Jann, even though people told Salter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.740
that it wasn't his fault, he was never able to&nbsp;
fully let it go and it caused him to struggle to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:15.000
get back into the driver's seat. To this day,&nbsp;
Salter still regrets it and doesn't want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.200
see Jann go down the same path. Salter's&nbsp;
story ends up inspiring Jann to not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.400
reignite his racing career but also achieve&nbsp;
the dreams that were cut short for Salter.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.500
Although Jann is ready to return to racing,&nbsp;
Danny gives him some unfortunate news. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.340
Jann isn't seen as responsible for the&nbsp;
accident, others would rather have him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.120
no longer race. Most of the other drivers&nbsp;
have signed a petition to keep "simulation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.380
racers" like Jann from competing -- causing&nbsp;
some of Jann's sponsors to consider pulling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.460
their support. With Jann not wanting to quit,&nbsp;
he comes up with a way for them to prove that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:49.680
he belongs -- by placing on the podium at the 24&nbsp;
Hours of Le Mans with a team of simulation racers.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.420
Salter and Danny agree with Jann and call for&nbsp;
two of his "GT Academy" adversaries to race&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:59.400
alongside him in a three-man team. Before the race&nbsp;
starts, Jann is also able to reconcile with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.480
father -- gaining the support and acceptance&nbsp;
he's yearned for. Jann struggles early in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:08.100
race after witnessing another driver crash, but&nbsp;
with the help of Salter reminding Jann of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.780
he's driving for, he's able to get in the right&nbsp;
headspace. Despite some issues with the pit crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.220
Jann is able to fight back in the race and&nbsp;
ultimately lead his team to a third place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:22.189
finish -- cementing their place in history and&nbsp;
squashing any doubt of their ability to perform.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.940
Shortly after Jann and his team celebrate&nbsp;
on the podium, the film delivers some small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.560
tidbits about Jann's real-life career and&nbsp;
involvement with the film. Alongside some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:35.820
photos of Jann's real experience competing&nbsp;
in "GT Academy" and driving professionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:41.220
the film acknowledges that Jann has competed&nbsp;
in over 200 races and earned many achievements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.780
in his career. As an added bonus, the film&nbsp;
even tells viewers that Jann actually acts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.414
as the stunt double for actor Archie Madekwe&nbsp;
in the film. However, the bigger question is:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.414 --> 00:03:53.520
How much of what we see in the film&nbsp;
is true to Jann's real-life story?

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.060
While certain characters like Jack&nbsp;
Salter are solely made up for the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.920
the events of the story are pretty accurate --&nbsp;
but somewhat told out of order. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.060
the catastrophic accident that caused Jann&nbsp;
to crash into a field of spectators actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.440
happened a couple of years after he placed&nbsp;
third at Le Mans. Also, he didn't race alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:15.833
other "GT Academy" graduates at Le Mans — he&nbsp;
raced with them at the Spa 24 hours instead.

00:04:15.833 --> 00:04:19.740
"I've been cynical as well, because&nbsp;
you have kids sitting in front of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:24.120
TV screens playing motor circuit&nbsp;
games, or whatever you call them."

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.080
So even though Jann's story in the film&nbsp;
is inspired by actual events in Jann's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.980
career rather than wholeheartedly based on&nbsp;
them, "Gran Turismo" does its best to pay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.690
tribute to the achievements and impact&nbsp;
Jann has had on the motorsport world.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.100
One of the biggest debates throughout the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.868
is whether simulation players&nbsp;
can hack it on a real track.

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:44.040
"Much easier with a joystick, isn't it? Ha ha ha."

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.300
That question is what drives Danny to&nbsp;
create "GT Academy" and causes Salter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.020
to openly doubt all the participants at&nbsp;
the start of the competition. Jann is at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.440
the center of this debate as well. He's&nbsp;
trying to prove his critics wrong and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.580
show that the "Gran Turismo" community should&nbsp;
be taken seriously. There are major hurdles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:04.296
for Jann and other "GT Academy" competitors,&nbsp;
but he eventually puts his doubters in check.

00:05:04.296 --> 00:05:08.220
When Jann enters the world of professional&nbsp;
racing, he's quite a force to be reckoned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.240
with. He continually improves his craft&nbsp;
and impresses people in his first race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.280
even though it doesn't end in victory. Jann is&nbsp;
living proof that simulation and video game skills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.840
can translate to reality and be a stepping stone&nbsp;
for someone wanting to be involved in the real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.700
thing. Moments including Jann knowing parts of the&nbsp;
car Salter didn't expect him to and understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:30.935
how to make passes on turns are great&nbsp;
instances of the game connecting with reality.

00:05:31.935 --> 00:05:33.648
"That was actually pretty great."

00:05:33.648 --> 00:05:37.440
The film further gives the "Gran Turismo"&nbsp;
community, and really every sim community,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.180
a voice and shows that they are very capable&nbsp;
of turning their virtual passions into reality.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:47.760
As much as "Gran Turismo" is a positive message&nbsp;
about chasing your dreams, it's also a bit of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.180
cautionary tale. Sure, there's a lot of&nbsp;
heartwarming success in Jann's journey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:56.160
but it doesn't overshadow how the film highlights&nbsp;
the dangers of motorsport. Before Jann even starts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.420
his "GT Academy" journey, Salter makes it&nbsp;
clear that students could potentially die&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.260
if things go wrong. He even says that there&nbsp;
would be no shame in quitting and that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:08.160
wouldn't let anyone he didn't believe in sit&nbsp;
in the driver's seat. At first, this seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.572
like an intimidation tactic from Salter, but&nbsp;
it quickly becomes clear that he's not wrong.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:16.620
The crashes in "Gran Turismo" prove how&nbsp;
vicious and genuinely deadly motorsport&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:21.240
can be. One wrong twitch during a turn or&nbsp;
slight hesitation can lead to the driver's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.620
death and the deaths of other drivers and&nbsp;
spectators. Jann experiences this multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:30.600
times throughout the film. He sees a fiery crash&nbsp;
at Le Mans that the driver miraculously survives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.352
and he himself is involved in a crash&nbsp;
that accidentally kills a spectator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.352 --> 00:06:38.100
Even the psychological trauma drivers&nbsp;
can suffer from is just as horrifying.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:42.710
"Gran Turismo" doesn't shy away from the&nbsp;
danger and potential tragedy of motorsport.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:48.180
At its core, "Gran Turismo" is a sports underdog&nbsp;
story meant not only to warm viewers' hearts but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:52.980
also to inspire them to pursue their passions.&nbsp;
Like any underdog, Jann faces his fair share of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:57.060
adversity. From his father disapproving&nbsp;
of his aspirations, becoming a racer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:01.740
and Salter doubting his ability throughout his&nbsp;
time at "GT Academy," there wasn't much support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:07.140
for Jann. Plus he has to face and ultimately beat&nbsp;
his "GT Academy" competitors, who were equally as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:11.640
talented. Even when he finally earns his chance&nbsp;
to race in professional circuits, he's looked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:16.172
down upon by other drivers and is forced to deal&nbsp;
with an accident that was beyond his control.

00:07:16.172 --> 00:07:21.000
Yet, Jann constantly perseveres and overcomes&nbsp;
the obstacles in front of him through his sheer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:26.100
determination. He always finds ways to push beyond&nbsp;
his limits and impress anyone who doubts him. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:30.240
father and Salter are certainly impressed&nbsp;
by his drive and ultimately become his most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.877
pivotal supporters. It's what makes Jann leading&nbsp;
a landmark performance at Le Mans so meaningful:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.877 --> 00:07:38.760
Audiences have been with him every step&nbsp;
of the way. "Gran Turismo" is a classic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:43.200
sports story with underdog vibes that remind&nbsp;
viewers that everyone's dreams can come true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:47.971
no matter how big or small. Buy more video&nbsp;
games, and you too could become world famous.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.440
The film ending on Jann Mardenborough's&nbsp;
legendary performance at the 24 Hours of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.980
Le Mans actually holds more meaning than&nbsp;
you'd think. At the start of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:00.000
Jann is racing his friend online in&nbsp;
"Gran Turismo" on the Le Mans track.

00:08:01.236 --> 00:08:02.676
"I know this track."

00:08:02.676 --> 00:08:06.660
So competing in the real-life endurance&nbsp;
race in the finale brings his journey full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:10.800
circle. Jann and his team placing third at&nbsp;
Le Mans is arguably one of his most notable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.520
achievements in his real-life professional&nbsp;
career. It was the race that really put him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:18.240
on the map and helped him break away from&nbsp;
being looked at as the "GT Academy" winner.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:22.200
Le Mans being the setting for the film's&nbsp;
finale is also meaningful for fans of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:27.420
sport and general fans since the race has an&nbsp;
iconic legacy in the sport. The 24 Hours of Le&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:31.140
Mans is easily one of the most well-known&nbsp;
and highly-regarded events in the racing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:35.700
world. As explained in the film, placing there&nbsp;
solidifies you as a legend in the sport. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.220
it's a setting that elevates&nbsp;
the meaning behind Jann and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:41.580
team trying to get "sim racers" like&nbsp;
themselves the respect they deserve.

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:44.880
So often these days, when&nbsp;
a big name movie premieres,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:49.920
audiences wonder if it has franchise potential.&nbsp;
At this point, Sony hasn't made any announcements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:54.240
regarding a sequel to "Gran Turismo," and&nbsp;
honestly there probably won't be one. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:58.713
movie is based on the real-life story of Jann&nbsp;
Mardenborough, and not strictly on the game.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.713 --> 00:09:03.240
Though a sequel could focus on Jann's career&nbsp;
after his origin story, that seems unlikely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:07.320
Another potential could be a movie that focuses&nbsp;
on another driver with a similar background.

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:11.700
Even more interesting could be a follow-up&nbsp;
that is completely original and not based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:15.960
on an actual racing figure. But the fact&nbsp;
that "Gran Turismo" is a biopic makes it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:19.980
unique in the world of video game movie&nbsp;
adaptations, so a fictionalized follow-up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:24.300
probably doesn't make sense for a potential&nbsp;
sequel. However, if Sony's new movie does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:28.440
well at the box office you can expect that&nbsp;
at least one executive will look for ways to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:32.569
bring the "Gran Turismo" name back to the&nbsp;
screen for another lap around the track.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.960
Although Sony and PlayStation have shown&nbsp;
interest in turning their movie and TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:41.460
adaptations of video games into successful&nbsp;
franchises, the ending of "Gran Turismo" says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:45.300
something different. While we already know that&nbsp;
a second season of "The Last of Us" is coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:48.840
and that the endings of "Uncharted" and&nbsp;
"Twisted Metal" hint at potential futures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:53.460
"Gran Turismo" is an adaptation that feels&nbsp;
complete. The ending highlights Jann's success&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:57.668
in the film and in real-life and doesn't&nbsp;
suggest that there's another story to tell.

00:09:57.668 --> 00:10:01.800
Since it seems like Sony isn't trying to&nbsp;
establish a big cinematic future for "Gran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:06.360
Turismo," it suggests that we could see smaller&nbsp;
adaptations in the future. PlayStation games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:11.760
like "Concrete Genie," "Ape Escape," "Shadow of&nbsp;
the Colossus," or maybe even "Patapon" could get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:16.380
big or small screen adaptations one day. Prior&nbsp;
to "Gran Turismo," we expected that PlayStation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:21.300
would try to turn all of their adaptations into&nbsp;
robust franchises. But "Gran Turismo" changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:25.628
that narrative with its ending and opens&nbsp;
the door for more potential adaptations.

